{
 "encounter_id": "00710",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello, doctor. I can't smell anything. It's the strangest thing. Nothing. I had a cold in September and it never came back."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long has it been?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Eleven weeks. I counted, because I'm a chef, and it's a nightmare. I can't taste, either. Everything tastes of cardboard."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is your nose blocked as well?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit, on the left, on and off. And a bit of post-nasal drip."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever, or pain in your face?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No fever, and no face pain."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any bang on the head before this started?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. I'd have remembered that. Oh, did I mention I've lost my keys?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's stick with the nose for now. What do you use for it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A steroid nasal spray, fluticasone, two sprays each nostril once a day, and cetirizine, 10 mg, for my hay fever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you have any other conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hay fever, as I said, and asthma."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any previous nose operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, my septum was straightened. Septoplasty. In 2015."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you smoke?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I gave up four years ago. Twenty a day, for years, before that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me take your pulse, pressure and so on. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 70, blood pressure 124 over 80, temperature 36.6, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 14 a minute.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'm all right then. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any wheeze or breathlessness, with the asthma?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, the asthma's quiet. No wheeze."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'm not going to give this a name just yet. A cold can damage the smell nerves for a time, and mostly it comes back, but at eleven weeks, I want to look properly. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to arrange a smell identification test, where you sniff a set of scratch-and-sniff cards."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That sounds fun. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'd like to arrange a CT scan of your sinuses, to check there's no blockage."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. Is it permanent? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Often not. Smell training, sniffing four strong scents twice a day, like rose, lemon, clove and eucalyptus, helps nerves recover."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've got those in the pantry. Cloves, lemon. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Perfect. Keep using the nasal spray, and make sure your smoke and gas alarms are working, since you can't smell a leak."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh, that's a good point. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks, after the tests."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Four weeks. Right. Thank you, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
